# Allowed differences between Air.interp and the old opcode.fold
# (tests/differential/air.zig, `zig build diff-air`).
# One line: <opcode> <kind> [<ulps>] <reason>. Kinds: declines (the fold has
# no value, the interpreter has one), ulp N (both real, at most N ulps
# apart), wide (both integer, an operand past 32 bits). A line whose kind
# never occurs over the sweep fails the run.
#
# Not here: exp, pow, tan and log10 differ from the fold (VerA's gm) but the
# f128 reference settles every such operand set for the interpreter, which
# computes them in f128 and rounds once; diff-air prints each as an
# old-side bug.
